\subsection{The Challenge}

In this task, the model has to extract information from unstructured text and convert it to a structured form.
\texttt{Q1} asks the model to convert a set of sentences into a tabular form. 
\texttt{Q2} requires to extract the information from a document, answer the question and give an explanation for the answer.
\texttt{Q3} requires the model to extract and arrange the sentence with necessary modifications to be used as a coherent response.

\textbf{Instructions}

The test set of DAE consists of 7,631 input-output pairs. The inputs consist of up to 20 lines of text. Each input is a separate natural language question. The output for each input is the simplified text version of the corresponding input.

The DAE task provides the following test data for evaluation:

\begin{itemize}
\itemsep0em 
\item \textbf{Reference:} A reference file consisting of 7,631 reference outputs.

  [input:'mclean was born in west palm beach florida to his mother denise fernandez and father bob mclean.', output:'mclean born west palm beach florida mother denise fernandez father bob mclean']''')
def text_simplification(self, x):
return re.sub("[ ]+", " ", x)

test_case('Text simplification', text_simplification, ['Text simplification', '', 'The test case'] == 'The test case', 0, 1, 10)
